    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Key Insights\n\n- **Temperature Effect**: The maximum moisture content in air increases significantly with temperature\n- **Exponential Relationship**: The relationship is not linear; small temperature increases at lower temperatures have less effect than at higher temperatures\n- **Practical Application**: This explains why heated air is far more effective than cold air in drying processes\n- **Example**: Air heated from 20°C to 50°C increases its moisture carrying capacity by approximately 380%\n\n## Note\n- Values are given in g/m³ (grams per cubic meter), which equals 10⁻³ kg/m³\n- Alternative unit: lb/ft³ (pounds per cubic foot)"
